{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"finance-report-analyzer","displayName":"Finance Report Analyzer","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/qiujiahong/skills/finance-report-analyzer","publisherHandle":"qiujiahong","publisherDisplayName":"Nick Qiu","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/qiujiahong","version":"1.2.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1772935228922,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/finance-report-analyzer/card?ownerHandle=qiujiahong&version=1.2.0","sha256":"c6083dd2649b2cc75ec85320da711e5cf202c4731d4a3130a674c71f952ebd58","size":2429,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"b1e897036be98d2d7af3ba6f56d5100cb7034212e1138347ce9f2c04ba600360","bundleFingerprints":["006ee5337263fdff5a53121330f2f0bb74b0e0c97ab299e139fa1e71627790bd","f35fc2bde9c3db8853b16f5aa749120116b35ae4e71d71d76e8509ff3a3c82c6"],"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3688,"sha256":"ac1124fa046838c8e21f441a79bc5359c1841f1539a39d3f4ca3b5e1f325e590","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3753,"sha256":"838c42622a0bc513781cd6c5b98eb582488b46e6e82ca51a0dd6a48e4dcb7770","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/report-theme.css","size":243,"sha256":"4c3577faef7e5d00ce7536946fb4ba244c4040e0ca6d0ff008f0798d31948b1d","contentType":"text/css"},{"path":"references/metrics.md","size":1754,"sha256":"957458892cc283e09850584f28458fc7af760e99e1c1fead07cc2a15cbcb481e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/generate_report.py","size":31660,"sha256":"0723533aebcdb6a5a9c5ee0a307190d3c7d907a82d3a4b1de59572b48f205c15","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly generates finance reports, but it also directs use of local Feishu credentials, external file transfer, runtime package installation, and unsafe document conversion settings.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789114016565,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"error","message":{"text":"Automatic Installation of Unpinned Python Dependencies at Runtime"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/generate_report.py"},"region":{"startLine":16,"endLine":20}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"ad6eec529b8cd8be"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/generate_report.py:16-20` and `scripts/generate_report.py:691-701`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Runtime dependency installation without version or integrity controls  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\ntry:\n    import openpyxl\nexcept ImportError:\n    os.system(\"pip install openpyxl -q\")\n    import openpyxl\n```\n\n```python\ntry:\n    os.system(\"pip install markdownify -q\")\n    from markdownify import markdownify\n    with open(html_path) as f:\n        md = markdownify(f.read(), heading_style=\"ATX\")\n    with open(md_path, \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(md)\n    return True\nexcept:\n    return False\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe report generator automatically invokes `pip` when `openpyxl` or `markdownify` is unavailable. The packages are installed without:\n\n- An exact version pin\n- A cryptographic hash\n- A lockfile\n- Repository restrictions\n- Explicit user approval\n- Separation between installation and report processing\n\nPython package installation can execute package build and installation logic. Consequently, running the report generator may execute code retrieved from the configured Python package index with the same privileges as the user or Agent.\n\nThe use of `os.system` also inherits environment-dependent shell and pip behavior. A manipulated `PATH`, `PIP_INDEX_URL`, pip configuration, or package repository could change which executable or package is used.\n\nDependency installation is not necessary during financial-report processing. It therefore exceeds the minimum privileges and network activity required for the declared report-generation operation.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. The attacker compromises an upstream package, dependency, configured package index, or local pip configuration.\n2. The victim runs the report generator in an environment where `openpyxl` or `markdownify` is missing.\n3. The script automatically executes `pip install` without displaying or validating the resolved package version.\n4. Pip downloads and installs the attacker-controlled package or transitive dependency.\n5. Package installation or import executes attacker-controlled Python code.\n6. The payload receives the privileges of the Agent or user running the Skill.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation can provide arbitrary code execution under the report generator's operating account. This may allow access to:\n\n- Financial input files and generated reports\n- Files readable or writable by the Agent\n- Environment variables and locally stored credentials\n- Available network services\n- Feishu credentials if they are accessible in the execution environment\n\nThe code does not explicitly elevate to root. The obtainable scope is therefore limited by the privileges of the invoking process, but those privileges may still include sensitive business data and messaging credentials.\n]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Remove every runtime `pip install` invocation.\n2. Declare dependencies in a dedicated project manifest and lockfile.\n3. Pin exact package versions and require cryptographic hashes, for example through a hash-locked requirements file.\n4. Install dependencies in a separate, explicit setup phase:\n   ```bash\n   python3 -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt\n   ```\n5. If a dependency is missing at runtime, terminate with a clear error rather than modifying the environment:\n   ```python\n   try:\n       import openpyxl\n   except ImportError as exc:\n       raise SystemExit(\n           \"Missing dependency: openpyxl. Install audited project dependencies first.\"\n       ) from exc\n   ```\n6. Restrict dependency retrieval to an approved repository or internal mirror.\n7. Run installation and report generation in separate, unprivileged virtual environments or containers.\n8. Review and update locked dependencies through a controlled maintenance process.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Unescaped Input Rendered with Weakened Browser and Local-File Security Controls"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/generate_report.py"},"region":{"startLine":470,"endLine":479}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"d0259cbabaf41592"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/generate_report.py:412`, `scripts/generate_report.py:470-479`, `scripts/generate_report.py:503-505`, `scripts/generate_report.py:548-550`, and `scripts/generate_report.py:662-673`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: HTML injection combined with unsafe document-renderer configuration  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\nSpreadsheet header values are copied into report dates without HTML escaping:\n\n```python\ndates = []\nfor i in indices:\n    h = str(header_row[i]) if i < len(header_row) and header_row[i] else \"\"\n    dates.append(h[:4] if len(h) >= 4 else h)\n```\n\nSpreadsheet values are interpolated directly into HTML:\n\n```python\nif is_pct:\n    r += f'<td{cls}>{val_cls_open}{fmt_pct(v)}{val_cls_close}{forecast_mark}</td>'\nelse:\n    fv = to_float(v)\n    color = \"\"\n    if fv is not None and not fc:\n        color = ' class=\"positive\"' if fv > 0 else ' class=\"negative\"' if fv < 0 else \"\"\n    elif fv is not None and fc:\n        color = ' class=\"positive forecast-val\"' if fv > 0 else ' class=\"negative forecast-val\"' if fv < 0 else ' class=\"forecast-val\"'\n    r += f'<td{cls}><span{color}>{fmt(v)}</span>{forecast_mark}</td>'\n```\n\nCLI-controlled company and ticker values are inserted into the page title:\n\n```python\nhtml = f\"\"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>{title} 财务分析报告</title>\n```\n\n```python\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"header\">\n<h1>📊 {title}</h1>\n<div class=\"subtitle\">财务分析报告 | 单位：亿元(CNY)</div>\n</div>\n```\n\nGenerated HTML is processed with local-file access enabled or browser sandboxing disabled:\n\n```python\ndef html_to_pdf(html_path, pdf_path):\n    for cmd in [\n        [\"wkhtmltopdf\", \"--quiet\", \"--enable-local-file-access\", \"--page-size\", \"A4\", \"--orientation\", \"Landscape\", html_path, pdf_path],\n    ]:\n        try:\n            subprocess.run(cmd, check=True, capture_output=True)\n            return True\n        except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):\n            pass\n    for browser in [\"chromium-browser\", \"chromium\", \"google-chrome\"]:\n        try:\n            subprocess.run([browser, \"--headless\", \"--disable-gpu\", \"--no-sandbox\", f\"--print-to-pdf={pdf_path}\", html_path], check=True, capture_output=True)\n            return True\n        except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):\n            continue\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe generated report treats spreadsheet contents and CLI arguments as trusted HTML. Values returned by `fmt()` remain strings when they cannot be parsed as numbers, allowing markup supplied in an Excel cell to reach the output document unchanged. Company and ticker arguments are likewise embedded directly in `<title>` and `<h1>` elements.\n\nAn attacker can therefore inject HTML elements, external resources, or scripts into the generated report. The script subsequently opens this report using browser-class converters with dangerous security reductions:\n\n- `wkhtmltopdf --enable-local-file-access` permits the renderer to access local files.\n- Chromium's `--no-sandbox` disables an important containment boundary for untrusted web content.\n\nThe precise ability to execute JavaScript or expose local file contents depends on the installed converter version and its runtime policies. Nevertheless, processing attacker-controlled HTML in this configuration creates a credible route to report manipulation, network requests, local-file access, and exploitation of browser or rendering-engine vulnerabilities.\n\nNeither local-file access nor disabling the browser sandbox is required for the report's declared functionality because the generated report uses inline CSS and inline SVG.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker provides a crafted Excel workbook or persuades the victim to use attacker-controlled `--company` or `--ticker` text.\n2. A spreadsheet cell or CLI argument contains malicious HTML, such as a remote-resource element, script-capable markup, or a local-file reference.\n3. `generate_html()` interpolates the value into the report without contextual HTML escaping.\n4. The victim requests PDF output, which is the default output mode.\n5. The script invokes wkhtmltopdf with local-file access enabled or Chromium with sandboxing disabled.\n6. The renderer parses the injected content.\n7. Depending on the renderer and payload, the attacker may trigger outbound requests, manipulate the resulting report, attempt to read accessible local resources, or exploit a rendering-engine vulnerability.\n8. If a renderer exploit succeeds, code runs with the privileges of the report-generation process.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe direct and reliable impact is arbitrary modification of report structure and presentation, including falsification or concealment of financial information.\n\nEnvironment-dependent additional impact includes:\n\n- Requests to attacker-controlled network endpoints\n- Disclosure of locally readable files through renderer-supported resource loading\n- Exposure of sensitive report data or local credentials\n- Browser or wkhtmltopdf compromise through renderer vulnerabilities\n- Arbitrary code execution as the user or Agent when combined with a suitable renderer exploit\n\nThe implementation does not itself obtain administrator privileges. The scope is bounded by the operating-system privileges, file access, and network access of the process. However, disabling the Chromium sandbox materially increases the consequences of a renderer compromise.\n]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Escape every external value before inserting it into HTML:\n   ```python\n   from html import escape\n\n   safe_company = escape(str(company), quote=True)\n   safe_ticker = escape(str(ticker), quote=True)\n   safe_value = escape(fmt(v), quote=True)\n   safe_date = escape(str(date), quote=True)\n   ```\n2. Apply contextual escaping to spreadsheet labels, headers, values, company names, ticker symbols, titles, and any future web-search content.\n3. Validate fields against strict schemas:\n   - Permit expected numeric formats for financial values.\n   - Permit only expected year/date formats for report headers.\n   - Restrict ticker symbols to a narrow allowlist pattern.\n   - Apply reasonable length limits to all text fields.\n4. Remove `--enable-local-file-access` from wkhtmltopdf. If a local resource is essential, copy it into a dedicated temporary directory and allow access only to that directory through a constrained mechanism.\n5. Remove Chromium's `--no-sandbox` option.\n6. Disable JavaScript and block remote resource loading during conversion wherever supported.\n7. Run document conversion in a dedicated unprivileged container or sandbox with:\n   - No access to credentials\n   - No access to unrelated host files\n   - A read-only filesystem except for dedicated input/output directories\n   - Network access disabled\n   - CPU, memory, and execution-time limits\n8. Keep the rendering engine patched and avoid obsolete wkhtmltopdf builds.\n9. Add security tests using crafted workbook cells containing HTML tags, scripts, remote URLs, and `file://` references to verify that the output contains escaped text only.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":20,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789113761.797201,"endTime":1789113967.2952323}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"finance-report-analyzer","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v572cqcm6jsx8fka3wf4t87mwh8e6npw-My3SWO/clawscan-skillspector-4081331350/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T08:02:41.169815+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":113,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3688,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":97,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3753,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"assets/report-theme.css","type":"other","lines":11,"executable":false,"size_bytes":243,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/metrics.md","type":"markdown","lines":51,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1754,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/generate_report.py","type":"python","lines":740,"executable":true,"size_bytes":31660,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-fe6969eb9b814eb88b0a53854c905124","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The core purpose mostly aligns: the script performs financial analysis and creates rich reports with sparkline-like trend charts, and it supports HTML/PDF/DOCX/Markdown outputs. However, the declared description overstates supported inputs and triggers. The actual code only accepts a local Excel file path and parses .xlsx with openpyxl; there is no code for reading PDF files, CSV files, stock ticker lookup, or Feishu links/docs. Thus the description is not fully accurate and includes materially undeclared input capabilities that are absent from the code.","remediation":"Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/generate_report.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":740,"actual_behavior_summary":"Code reads only Excel workbooks via openpyxl, extracts financial rows, generates an HTML financial analysis report with inline SVG sparklines and narrative analysis, and optionally converts the HTML to PDF, DOCX, or Markdown using external tools."},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC2","finding_id":"finding-4521a0b92df14d07a5c535cb27f51713","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"External Script Fetching","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":38,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s -X POST 'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal' \\\n     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n     -d '{\"app_id\":\"APP_ID\",\"app_secret\":\"APP_SECRET\"}' | python","explanation":"Remote code is downloaded and executed. This bypasses code review and could introduce malicious code.","remediation":"Avoid downloading and executing remote scripts. Use trusted packages from PyPI/npm. If remote fetch is required, verify checksums and use HTTPS.","code_snippet":"1. **Feishu chat file attachment** — Download via API:\n   ```bash\n   # Get token\n   TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST 'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal' \\\n     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n     -d '{\"app_id\":\"APP_ID\",\"app_secret\":\"APP_SECRET\"}' | python3 -c \"import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['tenant_access_token'])\")\n   # Get file_key from message","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"a69089b97fb772762ecab9cdf5c8a271fba0337df2e8b5132215ce86bf00b393","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":38,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC2","finding_id":"finding-e3d8b21307c34002a88b3c72dee26cb5","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"External Script Fetching","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":42,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages/{message_id}\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\n   # Download\n   curl -s \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages/{message_id}/resource","explanation":"Remote code is downloaded and executed. This bypasses code review and could introduce malicious code.","remediation":"Avoid downloading and executing remote scripts. Use trusted packages from PyPI/npm. If remote fetch is required, verify checksums and use HTTPS.","code_snippet":"     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n     -d '{\"app_id\":\"APP_ID\",\"app_secret\":\"APP_SECRET\"}' | python3 -c \"import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['tenant_access_token'])\")\n   # Get file_key from message\n   curl -s \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages/{message_id}\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\n   # Download\n   curl -s \"https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages/{message_id}/resources/{file_key}?type=file\" \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -o /tmp/data.xlsx","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5e3202f4da3125610f41fc579623f7e2e615620ec5fc4cc46d2099285b646724","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":42,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-afb9fae38e2c40ba8dfb6870cad64689","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":47,"end_line":47},"finding":null,"explanation":"Directing the agent to retrieve app credentials from local configuration and use them to access and transmit files establishes a powerful secret-to-network path. In this context, the skill processes uploaded financial data, so the combination materially increases the risk of unauthorized access and exfiltration.","remediation":"Prohibit skills from reading local secret stores such as openclaw.json. Replace this with least-privilege, platform-scoped credentials and enforce policies that block arbitrary authenticated uploads/downloads from skill-authored instructions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":47,"end_line":47}]},{"id":"AST5","finding_id":"finding-094911f9ccff4d5eb5f9d9fb16656164","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"os.system() or os exec-family call","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":19,"end_line":19},"finding":"    os.system(\"pip install openpyxl -q\")","explanation":"The script installs Python packages at runtime using os.system(\"pip install ...\"), which executes a shell command and mutates the environment during normal operation. This creates supply-chain and environment integrity risk, and in this skill context it is more dangerous because the agent processes untrusted user files and should not also be fetching and executing code from package registries at runtime.","remediation":"Remove all runtime package installation logic. Declare dependencies in a pinned requirements file or package manifest, install them during build/deployment only, and fail closed with a clear error if a dependency is missing at runtime.","code_snippet":"try:\n    import openpyxl\nexcept ImportError:\n    os.system(\"pip install openpyxl -q\")\n    import openpyxl\n\n","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"639e777ee1fc37a386a30e85e8d11235c050a9a5c77d2e648896c799d83b9a3d","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":19,"end_line":19}]},{"id":"AST5","finding_id":"finding-bdb9944a5e3f493799ef3ac20c52f6a7","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"os.system() or os exec-family call","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":695,"end_line":695},"finding":"        os.system(\"pip install markdownify -q\")","explanation":"The Markdown fallback path installs markdownify at runtime via os.system(\"pip install ...\"), again executing a shell command and downloading code dynamically. This is dangerous because a report-generation utility should not alter the host or trust live package retrieval when processing user-supplied documents.","remediation":"Eliminate runtime installation from the Markdown path. Package markdownify as a declared dependency ahead of time, pin versions, and if unavailable return a controlled error instead of attempting installation.","code_snippet":"    except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):\n        pass\n    try:\n        os.system(\"pip install markdownify -q\")\n        from markdownify import markdownify\n        with open(html_path) as f:\n            md = markdownify(f.read(), heading_style=\"ATX\")","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"89da15f9e159ed35d2da3508216c36663d5678356fea3e2b500c23f7bc945e03","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":695,"end_line":695}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-63c7fc9b13144744b685b65a8eaf8754","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README advertises optional online benchmarking/search but does not disclose what data may be transmitted externally, which is important because users may upload sensitive financial statements or company data. In a finance-analysis skill, undisclosed network use can lead to unintended data exposure to third-party services or logs, especially when users expect local document processing.","remediation":"Document all outbound network behavior clearly in the README and SKILL docs, including what inputs or derived data may be sent, to which services, and under what conditions. Add an explicit opt-in flag for online benchmarking, provide a local-only mode by default, and warn users not to enable network features for confidential financial data unless they approve the disclosure.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-e9468e61bc54430da1e7aaed0bf4ff8e","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill uses shell commands and writes files but declares no explicit tool scope or permissions boundaries. That increases the blast radius because an agent may invoke broader capabilities than users expect, especially in a workflow that handles local files and external APIs.","remediation":"Add explicit allowed-tools/permissions for only the minimum required capabilities, such as tightly scoped file read/write and specific network access. Document why each capability is needed and deny shell access unless it is strictly necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-dd1219a397e940ad9016b13dad8142a2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":47},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs the agent to read Feishu app credentials from local configuration and use them for direct API access. That is dangerous because it normalizes secret retrieval from local files and enables authenticated access to external systems without clear user consent or platform mediation.","remediation":"Remove instructions to fetch secrets from local configuration inside the skill. Use platform-managed credential injection with explicit consent and narrow scopes, and require user-visible disclosure before any authenticated external access.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":47}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-abc861fa44584d028fcbef330ce14b0e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":47},"finding":null,"explanation":"The workflow accesses credentials and transmits user files to Feishu APIs without any user-facing warning about secret use or external data transfer. This undermines informed consent and may expose confidential financial documents to third-party services unexpectedly.","remediation":"Add clear user disclosure before retrieving credentials or sending any data externally, including what data will be sent and to which service. Require explicit opt-in and provide a local-only processing path by default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":47}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-e42087e834bf412cae30bfb08ed5bf9c","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":38,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s -X POST 'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal' \\\n     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n     -d ","explanation":"This command initiates authenticated external communication to Feishu to obtain an access token. External transmission is not always malicious, but here it is risky because it is paired with local secret use and can enable broader outbound data access.","remediation":"Restrict outbound network access to approved connectors instead of raw curl commands. Use managed authentication flows and log all external requests involving user data or local credentials.","code_snippet":"1. **Feishu chat file attachment** — Download via API:\n   ```bash\n   # Get token\n   TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST 'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal' \\\n     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n     -d '{\"app_id\":\"APP_ID\",\"app_secret\":\"APP_SECRET\"}' | python3 -c \"import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['tenant_access_token'])\")\n   # Get file_key from message","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5ea92d00694d4158e796c46f726691ef56f5e7ed15b9720db39ce48412801489","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":38,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-11a3cd8d4948495b803693b6c3dddb21","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":85},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill includes direct Feishu upload and message-sending steps that are not essential to the core report-generation logic. Embedding outbound file-delivery instructions creates an unnecessary data exfiltration channel for generated reports and any sensitive financial content they contain.","remediation":"Separate report generation from message delivery, and only allow outbound sharing through approved, audited platform tools. If delivery is necessary, require explicit user confirmation and limit destinations to the current conversation context.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":85}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-899358892d95497ba6f207b930560aac","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":85},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill tells the agent to upload generated reports to Feishu and send them as file messages, but does not warn that report contents leave the local environment. In a finance-analysis context, these files may include highly sensitive corporate or personal financial information.","remediation":"Present a user-visible confirmation before any report upload, with destination details and a summary of data being transmitted. Prefer returning the file locally through native platform attachment mechanisms instead of direct external API calls.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":85}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-15a92eb8a32a42feb3a7a56e6d78225d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":85},"finding":null,"explanation":"The workflow explicitly creates a path for uploaded financial content to be repackaged into reports and transmitted through Feishu APIs. Because the skill's domain is financial analysis, the transmitted data is likely to be sensitive, making this more dangerous than generic file sharing guidance.","remediation":"Remove direct API-based transmission from the skill, or gate it behind strict consent, audited destinations, and data-classification checks. Ensure sensitive reports are delivered only through approved in-product channels with logging and policy enforcement.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":67,"end_line":85}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-8d3ee2bb98e14b308caaad6c5f2e619d","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":81,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s -X POST 'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages?receive_id_type=chat_id' \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d ","explanation":"This command sends a file message through the Feishu API, creating a direct outbound channel for generated reports. In a financial-report skill, this can expose confidential financial analysis or source-derived content to external recipients if triggered without clear authorization.","remediation":"Replace direct curl-based message sending with a governed platform delivery mechanism that enforces recipient validation and user confirmation. Block external file transmission by default unless the user explicitly requests it.","code_snippet":"FILE_KEY=$(echo \"$UPLOAD\" | python3 -c \"import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['data']['file_key'])\")\n\n# 2. Send file message to chat\ncurl -s -X POST 'https://open.feishu.cn/open-apis/im/v1/messages?receive_id_type=chat_id' \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d \"{\\\"receive_id\\\":\\\"CHAT_ID\\\",\\\"msg_type\\\":\\\"file\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"file_key\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"$FILE_KEY\\\\\\\"}\\\"}\"","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c014c79d9e5db0a83cdfea574832838c130fc9d1718b80f3797eaf55e4feed8f","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":81,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-b4d8a3653c7d4b59baac559b5be61770","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":19,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"Runtime package installation is not necessary for the declared purpose of financial report generation and introduces environment-modifying behavior plus remote code supply-chain exposure. In an agent skill that handles user-provided files, this unnecessary capability broadens the attack surface significantly.","remediation":"Preinstall and pin dependencies during build or deployment. Remove all self-install behavior and replace it with explicit dependency checks and user-visible setup instructions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":19,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-8d28222f72044066badfc1e7cfb0697d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":501,"end_line":501},"finding":null,"explanation":"The HTML output explicitly sets lang=\"zh-CN\", and the surrounding generated report content is also fixed in Chinese throughout the file. This forces a specific language/locale without any opt-in or configuration mechanism, matching the language/locale policy violation criteria.","remediation":"Add a command-line option or configuration setting to choose output language/locale, or clearly document that the skill is intentionally restricted to zh-CN for a justified regional use case.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":501,"end_line":501}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-8ff3870b49bd47c7ab18c9523dcc33b4","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":667,"end_line":667},"finding":"            subprocess.run(cmd, check=True, capture_output=True)","explanation":"The wkhtmltopdf conversion executes an external renderer on generated HTML derived in part from workbook content and explicitly enables local file access. In this context, untrusted spreadsheet text can flow into HTML without escaping, making the renderer step more dangerous because it may process attacker-controlled markup with access to local files.","remediation":"HTML-escape all untrusted workbook and metadata content before embedding it in the report, disable --enable-local-file-access unless absolutely required, and run document conversion in a sandboxed, low-privilege environment.","code_snippet":"        [\"wkhtmltopdf\", \"--quiet\", \"--enable-local-file-access\", \"--page-size\", \"A4\", \"--orientation\", \"Landscape\", html_path, pdf_path],\n    ]:\n        try:\n            subprocess.run(cmd, check=True, capture_output=True)\n            return True\n        except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):\n            pass","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"476ce9e4572a7eaa832c0c7719ec78e0ccc4f56409fd9187fdb4c19ece3c5f64","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":667,"end_line":667}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-f2e606a7d8fa49aca0deaabc373be729","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.76,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":673,"end_line":673},"finding":"            subprocess.run([browser, \"--headless\", \"--disable-gpu\", \"--no-sandbox\", f\"--print-to-pdf={pdf_path}\", html_path], check=True, capture_output=True)","explanation":"Launching a headless browser with --no-sandbox to render attacker-influenced HTML materially weakens isolation. Because the HTML report includes unescaped content from input spreadsheets and company/ticker fields, this conversion step increases the risk that malicious HTML/JS or browser parsing bugs could impact the host.","remediation":"Do not use --no-sandbox. Escape all untrusted content before generating HTML, disable script execution if possible, and run browser-based rendering inside a hardened container or separate unprivileged worker.","code_snippet":"            pass\n    for browser in [\"chromium-browser\", \"chromium\", \"google-chrome\"]:\n        try:\n            subprocess.run([browser, \"--headless\", \"--disable-gpu\", \"--no-sandbox\", f\"--print-to-pdf={pdf_path}\", html_path], check=True, capture_output=True)\n            return True\n        except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):\n            continue","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"123c6f49e9d3e5d1d9df4b5f248be783c17999b96a46ecc48b618201ef3f0f1e","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":673,"end_line":673}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-7cd277aa04b0466c87824b0fbef79444","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":682,"end_line":682},"finding":"        subprocess.run([\"pandoc\", html_path, \"-o\", docx_path, \"--from=html\"], check=True, capture_output=True)","explanation":"subprocess module calls execute external commands. Without careful input validation, this enables command injection.","remediation":"Use subprocess.run() with shell=False and an explicit argument list. Validate all inputs and avoid passing user-controlled data to commands.","code_snippet":"\ndef html_to_docx(html_path, docx_path):\n    try:\n        subprocess.run([\"pandoc\", html_path, \"-o\", docx_path, \"--from=html\"], check=True, capture_output=True)\n        return True\n    except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):\n        return False","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b70f6c6c92d7282e9e12c62db443d1b3af33ac8f7d7d786fd4f3494210edbaf3","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":682,"end_line":682}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-fc5dc0b1ab6e47a6b35fa43691f44ba5","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":690,"end_line":690},"finding":"        subprocess.run([\"pandoc\", html_path, \"-o\", md_path, \"--from=html\", \"--to=gfm\"], check=True, capture_output=True)","explanation":"subprocess module calls execute external commands. Without careful input validation, this enables command injection.","remediation":"Use subprocess.run() with shell=False and an explicit argument list. Validate all inputs and avoid passing user-controlled data to commands.","code_snippet":"\ndef html_to_markdown(html_path, md_path):\n    try:\n        subprocess.run([\"pandoc\", html_path, \"-o\", md_path, \"--from=html\", \"--to=gfm\"], check=True, capture_output=True)\n        return True\n    except (FileNotFoundError, subprocess.CalledProcessError):\n        pass","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"12f03420f580ccfb77c36d10323dbae3bc98031f3c1b4406f52ee027ad13aa6f","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":690,"end_line":690}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-ad86e6cce0294bed845a6a1cb88510b9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":695,"end_line":700},"finding":null,"explanation":"The Markdown conversion fallback changes the host environment by installing a package on demand, which is unrelated to safe document transformation at runtime. This unnecessarily grants the script a code-fetching and execution path from an external repository.","remediation":"Ship markdownify as a predeclared dependency or remove the fallback entirely. Ensure runtime behavior is deterministic and does not download or install code.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":695,"end_line":700}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-82b5925684a8429ab64361af27a62424","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":3,"end_line":109},"finding":null,"explanation":"Nearly all user-facing documentation is presented only in Chinese, while the file does not state that the skill is intended exclusively for a Chinese-speaking or region-specific audience. Under the language/locale policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in or justification is a natural-language policy concern.","remediation":"Provide bilingual documentation, add an explicit language-selection note, or document that the skill is intended for a specific Chinese-language/regulatory context so the locale restriction is justified.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":3,"end_line":109}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-902ff5c1df8c4989b3f519540d56c5ca","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"references/metrics.md","start_line":1,"end_line":51},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown reference uses substantial Chinese-language content alongside English headings and labels, which can impose a language/locale constraint on users without explicit opt-in. Under the policy rule, forcing a specific language is a natural-language policy concern unless the file offers a choice or clearly justifies the locale scope.","remediation":"State that the reference is intended for Chinese-language financial analysis, or provide an English-only version / bilingual guidance with an explicit language choice for users.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/metrics.md","start_line":1,"end_line":51}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-42525be4c5a34204a52da3d3594e8d93","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":662,"end_line":682},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script runs wkhtmltopdf, Chromium/Chrome, and pandoc as child processes, which is a safety-relevant operation for code files. Although conversion is part of the skill's purpose, there is no visible pre-execution disclosure in code comments, docstrings, or user-facing output that local external programs will be executed.","remediation":"Add a short docstring, comment, or print message stating that report conversion relies on external tools and will execute local binaries such as wkhtmltopdf, Chromium, or pandoc.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":662,"end_line":682}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-120d5f414a194d82b5ea05065ae588b0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":722,"end_line":724},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code writes a generated HTML report to the filesystem and may also create the output directory earlier, but the only disclosure comes after the write succeeds. For this rule, file-writing behavior should have some prior user-facing disclosure, confirmation, or explanatory comment/docstring warning users that report files will be created in the specified directory.","remediation":"Add a brief user-facing warning before writing files, such as a print statement announcing the target paths and that existing files may be overwritten. Optionally require confirmation before overwriting an existing report file.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,